    <maml:alertSet>
      <maml:alert>
        <maml:para>This command writes deployment status to the host and starts workflow tasks. In GUI mode, workflow execution starts only after the operator clicks Start. Runtime parameters are provided by Get-OSDCloudWorkflowRuntimeParameter.</maml:para>
        <maml:para>Disk labels and sizes apply to registered CLI and GUI launches without new GUI controls. Unregistered deployments warn once when customization is supplied and use defaults. Sizes are bytes; PowerShell expressions such as 500MB or 100GB use binary units. Invalid input still fails parameter binding, while valid unregistered customization is discarded before capacity checks. Layouts that cannot fit the target disk fail before disk clearing. Capacity checks include system, MSR, enabled recovery, and alignment/metadata allowance.</maml:para>
      </maml:alert>
    </maml:alertSet>
